2186045417 true] [17592186413437 1079 #uuid "8dd2d3fa-c650-5e37-9b97-e79bceb3c6ba" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413421 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413423 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413427 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413433 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1077 "field-2" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413433 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413438 1079 #uuid "9b93007b-725a-5c21-aef1-4108c8c123fb" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413435 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413436 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1069 "q-338917" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1071 "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9\\lambda y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1072 #uuid "827b7203-4bc8-5ef4-ada5-12343dfe7439" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true] [17592186413439 1074 "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions ${y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields $A=0.$ Thus, we have a nontrivial solution, so $\\lambda =0$ is a parameter corresponding to eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+9\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 3\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $B=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n9\\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{81}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" 13194139534188 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0e54c974-6252-5708-b98d-d9bcad440480" 17592186413419 "answer-28512bc4-3366-5851-ab15-e9ddf7bdc6ed" 17592186413420 "answer-2ed3b012-ea23-5630-95d6-c16372fcd823" 17592186413421 "answer-333487d5-2b4f-53f7-a1f4-c935ce9920e2" 17592186413422 "answer-33bd6051-1ce7-59a0-a89b-5f289fa49519" 17592186413423 "answer-3a127422-744b-580f-8766-eedd4918927a" 17592186413424 "answer-3b6a8205-b73b-5687-a756-4e7c12880207" 17592186413425 "answer-3d8a953c-29a1-5c31-b0ad-482482bf1033" 17592186413426 "answer-408a492f-a860-5962-a306-84c6d1f01f6b" 1759218